(1864327, 254540, 24951, '<td valign="top">Wow! this is my best score ever! Thanks everyone for the great comments. My first Top 10! What makes this really sweet is that it was a member''s challenge, - so this pic is competing with images from great minds/artists/technicians/photographers all rolled into one. <br/> <br/>Ha Graphicfunk - I knew when I saw my score there would be a congratulatory comment by you first off. Thanks for taking the time!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-11-14 06:46:15.</i></td>', 'Wow! this is my best score ever! Thanks everyone for the great comments. My first Top 10! What makes this really sweet is that it was a member''s challenge, - so this pic is competing with images from great minds/artists/technicians/photographers all rolled into one.  Ha Graphicfunk - I knew when I saw my score there would be a congratulatory comment by you first off. Thanks for taking the time!', '2005-11-14 06:34:19.000000', '2005-11-14 06:46:15.000000', 0),
(1864332, 253499, 3306, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by elee3009:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats!  Figured this had to ribbon.  I''m totally fascinated by the fact you superglued all the bugs - does that include the one with its wings up - still can''t imagine how you did that.  Well-deserved evidently! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I used a pair of tweezers under the ladybugs wings to hold them up and then used the superglue under the wings to get them to stay. It took a while for the glue to dry so I was walking around the house with it. A strange site you can imagine! Getting this one to sit on top of the heap was the hardest part. He kept falling to the ground and getting the  positioning correct was difficult but perserverence paid off.</td>', 'Originally posted by elee3009: Congrats!  Figured this had to ribbon.  I''m totally fascinated by the fact you superglued all the bugs - does that include the one with its wings up - still can''t imagine how you did that.  Well-deserved evidently!   I used a pair of tweezers under the ladybugs wings to hold them up and then used the superglue under the wings to get them to stay. It took a while for the glue to dry so I was walking around the house with it. A strange site you can imagine! Getting this one to sit on top of the heap was the hardest part. He kept falling to the ground and getting the  positioning correct was difficult but perserverence paid off.', '2005-11-14 06:39:42.000000', NULL, 0),
