(1866763, 254446, 10080, '<td valign="top">I was one of your 4 tens daniel, and so, so underrated in my opinion. I would have never guessed it as your work, but I LOVED it!</td>', 'I was one of your 4 tens daniel, and so, so underrated in my opinion. I would have never guessed it as your work, but I LOVED it!', '2005-11-14 21:51:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1866800, 254561, 28276, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i> Technicals are quite nice.  Your focus is "spot on" as they like to say here.  I take it it''s f/4.0 not f/40. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>no... it was f/40...  using the 90mm macro and standing that close, that''s about as far as it goes in focus...  it was intentional.  i wanted the tip of the gun ''tack'' sharp and my face to be just be half out of focus, so i guess i got what i wanted ;)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i>I think it''s a decent picture.  It''s the subject which got you... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i think you''re right... i think the photo would have cleared 50% but for the subject, but i kinda knew that going in...  thanks...</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo: Technicals are quite nice.  Your focus is "spot on" as they like to say here.  I take it it''s f/4.0 not f/40.   no... it was f/40...  using the 90mm macro and standing that close, that''s about as far as it goes in focus...  it was intentional.  i wanted the tip of the gun ''tack'' sharp and my face to be just be half out of focus, so i guess i got what i wanted ;) Originally posted by DrAchoo:I think it''s a decent picture.  It''s the subject which got you...   i think you''re right... i think the photo would have cleared 50% but for the subject, but i kinda knew that going in...  thanks...', '2005-11-14 22:06:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1866818, 254397, 40718, '<td valign="top">Ok, I didn''t look at other comments, so this is all me.  By looking at the scores, you seem to have a done a good job with your idea, but the idea had limits.  In other words, this picture doesn''t really have the ability to soar (or in this case, perhaps, really creep people out).<br/> <br/>Although it is Time reaching for the subject, I''m not sure the wristwatch helps the picture.  The picture probably suffers the most from low contrast in an attempt to be low-key.  I goofed a bit in PS and think the picture looks better with the following change (you can try this in PS).  Boost contrast by +70 and lower brightness by -7.  It''s really rough, but I think this has more punch.<br/> <br/>A final confusing portion to the photo is why Time has chosen to catch up with this gal in her undies in a basement.  What are you trying to say here?</td>', 'Ok, I didn''t look at other comments, so this is all me.  By looking at the scores, you seem to have a done a good job with your idea, but the idea had limits.  In other words, this picture doesn''t really have the ability to soar (or in this case, perhaps, really creep people out). Although it is Time reaching for the subject, I''m not sure the wristwatch helps the picture.  The picture probably suffers the most from low contrast in an attempt to be low-key.  I goofed a bit in PS and think the picture looks better with the following change (you can try this in PS).  Boost contrast by +70 and lower brightness by -7.  It''s really rough, but I think this has more punch. A final confusing portion to the photo is why Time has chosen to catch up with this gal in her undies in a basement.  What are you trying to say here?', '2005-11-14 22:11:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1866842, 254518, 43671, '<td valign="top">I guess there is no place like home. YAY! Must be fun doing shots like this.</td>', 'I guess there is no place like home. YAY! Must be fun doing shots like this.', '2005-11-14 22:21:21.000000', NULL, 0),
