(1878950, 253784, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Dead End - The Gorge" a perfect title for this shot, also this is one hundred percent meeting the challenge.  What an amazing shot.  I am so glad that you included the truck to show the perspective of how large the the gorge truly is.  I know there have been comments about the truck.  I think if it was not included I would have possibly question why this would be an dead end, except that the road ran out.  I might have played with the contrast a little to see if you could bring some blue to the sky or possibly try a polarizing filter.  Also I was surprised the truck wasn''t close to the edge but after reading the description it makes complete sense.  The lighting on the top of the cliff is very nice for the shot. Personally I am surprised you didn''t finish higher, I think voters my have been looking for the drastic.  I bet if you jumped the truck you would have a ribbon, just kidding. Great job on the photo!</td>', '*Critique Club* "Dead End - The Gorge" a perfect title for this shot, also this is one hundred percent meeting the challenge.  What an amazing shot.  I am so glad that you included the truck to show the perspective of how large the the gorge truly is.  I know there have been comments about the truck.  I think if it was not included I would have possibly question why this would be an dead end, except that the road ran out.  I might have played with the contrast a little to see if you could bring some blue to the sky or possibly try a polarizing filter.  Also I was surprised the truck wasn''t close to the edge but after reading the description it makes complete sense.  The lighting on the top of the cliff is very nice for the shot. Personally I am surprised you didn''t finish higher, I think voters my have been looking for the drastic.  I bet if you jumped the truck you would have a ribbon, just kidding. Great job on the photo!', '2005-11-17 23:45:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1879012, 253223, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Wow this was one of my favorites, it is one of the most fitting for a Dead End challenge. I think a lot us probably thought wow a prison shot would be prefect (especially with the popularity of Prison Break on Fox) but who has access to a prison?  Thank goodness it was you.  This shot is set up very well.  I think the man''s expression and way he is stand greatly enhances the shot.  I also really like the you included the Silence During Lock Down as well as the shadows of the bars on the floor.  I really don''t see anything I would change.  Its a dark image but its not like you could make this a light or bright image.  Good job, especially working with the surrounds and lighting.</td>', '*Critique Club* Wow this was one of my favorites, it is one of the most fitting for a Dead End challenge. I think a lot us probably thought wow a prison shot would be prefect (especially with the popularity of Prison Break on Fox) but who has access to a prison?  Thank goodness it was you.  This shot is set up very well.  I think the man''s expression and way he is stand greatly enhances the shot.  I also really like the you included the Silence During Lock Down as well as the shadows of the bars on the floor.  I really don''t see anything I would change.  Its a dark image but its not like you could make this a light or bright image.  Good job, especially working with the surrounds and lighting.', '2005-11-17 23:58:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1879081, 253723, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Ok "FIRE!!" is what I would consider and excellent example of Depth of Field.  I think voters in this challenge were just looking for something dramatic, like some one jump off a bloody bridge.  I think the photo you have taken is excellent. Personally I like the image and what it states.  I think you did an excellent job with the focus and allowing the background to fade away but still leave  the bright colored background.  Personally I don''t see anything I would change at all.  Maybe if we had a history or revolution challenge, it would have faired better.</td>', '*Critique Club* Ok "FIRE!!" is what I would consider and excellent example of Depth of Field.  I think voters in this challenge were just looking for something dramatic, like some one jump off a bloody bridge.  I think the photo you have taken is excellent. Personally I like the image and what it states.  I think you did an excellent job with the focus and allowing the background to fade away but still leave  the bright colored background.  Personally I don''t see anything I would change at all.  Maybe if we had a history or revolution challenge, it would have faired better.', '2005-11-18 00:29:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1879193, 253499, 45920, '<td valign="top">i really like the way you took this, the close up and the way there up aganist each other GREAT JOB!</td>', 'i really like the way you took this, the close up and the way there up aganist each other GREAT JOB!', '2005-11-18 01:38:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1879219, 254084, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Very different approach, I do like the lighting.  I really like your perspective, who is behind these line us or her?  It very interesting that you had her placed in the cross lines and her eyes are boxed perfectly.  I think maybe the shot had a harder time in the Dead End category because its more of a hold position in my opinion.  It is s very interesting shot, I might play with cropping the shot and making it very full with the subject instead of all the surrounding area.  I do like you took a shot and defiantly took a different approach.</td>', '*Critique Club* Very different approach, I do like the lighting.  I really like your perspective, who is behind these line us or her?  It very interesting that you had her placed in the cross lines and her eyes are boxed perfectly.  I think maybe the shot had a harder time in the Dead End category because its more of a hold position in my opinion.  It is s very interesting shot, I might play with cropping the shot and making it very full with the subject instead of all the surrounding area.  I do like you took a shot and defiantly took a different approach.', '2005-11-18 01:49:38.000000', NULL, 0),
